# Markdown description continuation

## Root cause

The writer protects a leading `: ` in every paragraph. This changes unrelated corpus output, while the needed protection belongs to text continuing an open definition body.

## General change

When a paragraph is inside a definition description, protect a leading description separator on a continuation line. Keep the existing term marker handling for all paragraphs. This rule follows the AST parent and line position, not the text or indentation of corpus 657.

## Scope

Any definition body with a literal description-shaped continuation gets the same protection, including bodies nested in lists and other containers.
